    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Why the stock market doesn't like a hurry",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Why the stock market doesn't like a hurry"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-dlaczego-gielda-nie-lubi-pos.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In the short term, share prices react to news, crises and moods. They can fall **by tens of percent in a few months**."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you need the money in less than **2–3 years** (a car, a down payment, a holiday), the market may be in a dip just then – and you'll lock in a **real loss**."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "For the short term, choose a **savings account or a fixed deposit**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Current account vs savings account",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Current account vs savings account"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-konto-biezace-vs-oszczednosc.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each account has a different job:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Current account** – salary, card, transfers and bills. Usually **0%**",
                "**Savings account** (Tagesgeld) – for your emergency fund and near-term goals. It pays **interest** and gives access to your money at any time"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Don't keep spare money in your current account – there **inflation eats it**."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/c584ed85-3331-4ad2-a1f4-213cbf.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 220,
              "caption": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Fixed-term deposit",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Fixed-term deposit"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3i90sj.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **fixed deposit** (Festgeld) is a deal with the bank: you pay in an amount for a **set time** (e.g. 3, 6 or 12 months) and get a **fixed, known-in-advance** interest rate."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The money is **locked** – during that time you can't add to it or take it out."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Break the deposit early? You get your capital back, but you usually **lose the interest**. Only pay in money you definitely won't touch."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
